WEBVTT

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.096
You prefer that to audio-only

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.555
because you value having
the rich visual cues

00:18:32.579 --> 00:18:35.246
of facial expressions and body language.

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:37.793
That's how you read their emotions, right?

00:18:37.817 --> 00:18:40.346
(Imitates fail buzzer) Wrong.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:43.289
It turns out that if you want to know
what someone is feeling,

00:18:43.313 --> 00:18:45.912
you might be better off
just hearing their voice.

00:18:46.529 --> 00:18:47.695
In one experiment,

00:18:47.719 --> 00:18:50.225
people read another person's
emotions more accurately

00:18:50.249 --> 00:18:52.366
when the lights were turned off.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:53.547
In another experiment,

00:18:53.571 --> 00:18:56.706
they were more accurate
when the video feed was turned off.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:59.696
Follow-up studies showed
that when we don't have visual cues,

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:02.956
we pay more attention
to the content and tone of voice.